{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Split outbound_differ.py below the module-size cap (prerequisite for S3/S6)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`outbound_differ.py` sits at **799/800 LOC** — the hard module-size cap enforced by the\nCI-only gate in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` against `.github/module-size-limit.txt`\n(=800; strict `>`). S2 (438a) drove it to 799 via `repo_root` threading. S3 (`a8ea`,\nconfig-driven type mapping) and S6 (`d458`) both MUST add code here — S3 needs a `rebar-type:`\nstamp invocation site (mirroring the `rebar-status:` stamp invoked ~line 763) and per-project\ntype-skip threading through `compute_outbound_mutations` (~line 374, where `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`\nis loaded and passed to `_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets`). Any addition breaches 800 and\nfails CI `Verified`. This is a pure prerequisite refactor — no behaviour change.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract along an EXISTING call-graph seam (per AGENTS.md module-size policy — never\nmechanically, never a <100-LOC fragment). The two per-ticket mutation builders,\n`_compute_outbound_create_mutation` (lines 525–632, ~108 LOC) and\n`_compute_outbound_update_mutation` (lines 633–799, ~167 LOC), form a natural cluster: both are\ncalled ONLY by the `compute_outbound_mutations` orchestrator and both build a single\n`OutboundMutation` from a local/Jira ticket pair. Move the pair into a new sibling module\n`outbound_mutation_builders.py`. `compute_outbound_mutations` imports them back. Shared helpers\nthey use (`OutboundMutation`, `_load_config`, `_effective_status_map_for`, the mapper imports,\n`_best_effort`, `_is_retired`) either move with the cluster or are imported by the new module\nfrom `outbound_differ` / their existing homes — the implementer resolves the exact import edges\nso both modules type-check and no cycle forms. Result: `outbound_differ.py` ≈ 525 LOC, new\nmodule ≈ 290 LOC — both comfortably in the 200–500 target band.\n\nPublic API is unchanged: `compute_outbound_mutations`, `OutboundDiffConfig`, `OutboundMutation`\nkeep their import paths (re-export the mutation builders from `outbound_differ` if any test\nimports them by their private name). `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` mirrors the gate\nand must stay green.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` — remove the two builder functions;\n  import them from the new module; keep the orchestrator + dataclasses + top helpers.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py` (new) — the extracted\n  `_compute_outbound_create_mutation` + `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` cluster.\n\n## Testing\n\nPure behaviour-preserving refactor — the EXISTING outbound-differ suite is the oracle, run\nUNCHANGED (no new behavioural test is authored; a refactor that needs a new behavioural test\nwas not behaviour-preserving). The module-size contract test is the structural oracle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `outbound_differ.py` and `outbound_mutation_builders.py` are EACH < 800 LOC and within the\n  200–500 target band — verified by\n  `find src/rebar -name '*.py' | grep -v __pycache__ | xargs wc -l | awk '$1>800'` (empty) and\n  by `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` passing.\n- [x] The reconciler outbound suite passes GREEN unchanged — verified by\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ -k outbound` (no observable-behaviour change).\n- [x] The extraction is a single existing call-graph seam (the two `compute_outbound_mutations`\n  builders); no symbol's public import path changed (private-name importers get a re-export).\n\nTest tier: **refactor** — no new behaviour; the existing suite + the module-size contract are\nthe full oracle. Discovered during S3 (`a8ea`) plan-review round 1."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787351490195750001,"uuid":"75f02b1b-017a-4489-8f74-a780bff3f5a8"}